From 1be5b2dc7fcda16cff3d877858ccf40cae4f95fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 05:48:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): --origin-session binds cards an orchestrator
 creates to a chat on another gateway; missing kanban tool is a typed
 preflight failure [daveey]

A chat on gateway A handed a build to an orchestrator session on B. B's chat profile had no kanban
toolset, so the agent called the private kanban_create handler from a script; the cards were stamped
with B's one-shot session and A's chat lost them (empty task list, green row).

hermes chat --origin-session <ref> (or HERMES_ORIGIN_SESSION) now:
- registers the kanban toolset for that session (like dispatcher workers), so the real tool is there;
- validates the ref before anything runs: malformed, hub missing or a gateway hermes-hub does not know
  exit 2 with origin_ref_invalid / hub_not_installed / origin_gateway_unknown;
- preflight in tool assembly raises kanban_tool_unavailable instead of letting the agent fall back.
kanban_create (tool, new origin_session arg) and hermes kanban create (--origin-session) validate before
the card exists and add a platform='hub' subscription <gw>/<profile>/<session> (idempotent; children
inherit it), which hermes-hub publishes as rel:shepherd. The card's own session_id is not rewritten.
The result carries origin_binding {readback: pending, verify_on_origin: hermes-hub links ... --expect}.
